abla g_i( ar x):i\in I( ar x)\}\cup\{
abla h_j( ar x):1\le j\le p\}\) is linearly independent. MFCQ means that the equality gradients are linearly independent and some \(d\) satisfies \(\langle
abla h_j( ar x),dangle=0\) for all \(j\) and \(\langle
abla g_i( ar x),dangle<0\) for all \(i\in I( ar x)\). CRCQ means every subfamily of active inequality gradients together with the equality gradients has constant rank locally.

